WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.029 --> 00:00:02.312
- If it doesn't have a face,

00:00:02.312 --> 00:00:05.729
if it never had a face, would you eat it?

00:00:09.431 --> 00:00:10.435
- My name is Sara and I'm a

00:00:10.435 --> 00:00:11.946
video producer here at Buzzfeed

00:00:11.946 --> 00:00:15.080
and I just found out about lab grown meat.

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:19.648
So if you're like me, you're
thinking wait what is that?

00:00:19.648 --> 00:00:20.671
- What is it called?

00:00:20.671 --> 00:00:21.658
Is it like real meat?

00:00:21.658 --> 00:00:22.720
- Quick explainer.

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:24.908
Lab grown meat is actual meat,

00:00:24.908 --> 00:00:27.281
but they didn't slaughter
an animal to get it.

00:00:27.281 --> 00:00:28.814
- I guess it's like
cloned meat or something?

00:00:28.814 --> 00:00:30.670
- It's originally from
like an animal cell right,

00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:33.933
so they have to get something
from an animal to then grow.

00:00:33.933 --> 00:00:35.799
- Stem cells are taken from an animal

00:00:35.799 --> 00:00:37.655
and then they're grown in a culture.

00:00:37.655 --> 00:00:40.983
The cells multiply until
they become muscle tissue.

00:00:40.983 --> 00:00:43.454
- This looks like
somebody's getting pregnant.

00:00:43.454 --> 00:00:45.408
- That muscle tissue is what forms meat.

00:00:45.408 --> 00:00:48.492
Some of this sounds very
cool and sci-fi, right?

00:00:48.492 --> 00:00:50.990
But what are the benefits
of lab grown meat?

00:00:50.990 --> 00:00:53.012
According to the UN, meat consumption

00:00:53.012 --> 00:00:57.324
is expected to rise as
much as 73% by 2050.

00:00:57.324 --> 00:01:00.038
- Means we have like a
huge global food problem

00:01:00.038 --> 00:01:02.993
and so you know if it helps
solve that then awesome.

00:01:02.993 --> 00:01:06.613
- Growing meat in labs could
reduce greenhouse gases by 96%

00:01:06.613 --> 00:01:09.054
compared to traditional livestock farms.

00:01:09.054 --> 00:01:11.232
Are all of the benefits
from lab grown meat enough

00:01:11.232 --> 00:01:13.813
to convince a vegetarian
or vegan to try it?

00:01:13.813 --> 00:01:16.085
- I was raised without
any red meat or pork,

00:01:16.085 --> 00:01:17.700
so I think it would make me pretty sick.

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:19.335
- My stomach would immediately reject it

00:01:19.335 --> 00:01:21.538
and I would just vomit, so probably not.

00:01:21.538 --> 00:01:23.648
- Don't want to eat
meat anyway whether it's

00:01:23.648 --> 00:01:25.601
from an animal or grown in a lab.

00:01:25.601 --> 00:01:28.091
- Yeah I don't think I stopped eating meat

00:01:28.091 --> 00:01:29.772
because of the cruelty.

00:01:29.772 --> 00:01:32.180
I miss chicken, I miss cheese,
I miss all these things,

00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:34.324
I just my stomach can't
tolerate it anymore.

00:01:34.324 --> 00:01:35.838
- I think it's taking something from them

00:01:35.838 --> 00:01:38.365
that we don't need to take
away and why do we need to take

00:01:38.365 --> 00:01:41.980
a animal cell to then grow a burger

00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:45.598
if we have so many plant based options?

00:01:45.598 --> 00:01:47.531
- For a lot of vegetarians and vegans,

00:01:47.531 --> 00:01:49.493
it doesn't matter it's lab grown meat.

00:01:49.493 --> 00:01:51.381
They're not interested in meat period.

00:01:51.381 --> 00:01:54.498
But for the meat eaters,
there are also some concerns.

00:01:54.498 --> 00:01:56.635
- I would probably try it, lab grown meat.

00:01:56.635 --> 00:01:58.143
It's a little bit weird.

00:01:58.143 --> 00:01:59.737
- I would try it once, you know,

00:01:59.737 --> 00:02:01.968
'cause I think I would
try everything once.

00:02:01.968 --> 00:02:03.191
- But I guess it's no weirder

00:02:03.191 --> 00:02:05.936
than eating like an actual animal.

00:02:05.936 --> 00:02:07.593
- Look, you cook it, I'll eat it.

00:02:07.593 --> 00:02:11.155
- The fact that we eat animals
is a little weird anyway,

00:02:11.155 --> 00:02:13.152
'cause they're just like,

00:02:13.152 --> 00:02:14.172
they're not that different from people.

00:02:14.172 --> 00:02:16.468
Why do I eat meat?

00:02:16.468 --> 00:02:19.478
- If I knew that it was grown
in a lab I would still eat it.

00:02:19.478 --> 00:02:21.419
I have no standards when it comes to food.

00:02:21.419 --> 00:02:22.581
- I would be down as long as

00:02:22.581 --> 00:02:24.560
they can prove it's not a carcinogen.

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:26.508
As long as like 30 years from now people

00:02:26.508 --> 00:02:28.921
aren't growing arms out of
their heads or something.

00:02:28.921 --> 00:02:30.476
- It depends on how expensive it is.

00:02:30.476 --> 00:02:31.961
- I wouldn't pay more money to eat food

00:02:31.961 --> 00:02:33.101
that was grown in a lab just

00:02:33.101 --> 00:02:35.617
because it didn't kill any animals.

00:02:35.617 --> 00:02:36.450
I'm broke.

00:02:37.853 --> 00:02:41.126
- Yeah lab grown meat
it sounds pretty fancy.

00:02:41.126 --> 00:02:42.669
It has to be expensive right?

00:02:42.669 --> 00:02:43.938
Like how much does it cost?

00:02:43.938 --> 00:02:46.771
- The current hamburger has costed

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:51.059
250,000 euro which is quite a lot.

00:02:51.059 --> 00:02:53.306
- Dr. Mark Post's lab grown hamburger

00:02:53.306 --> 00:02:55.973
cost $331,000 to produce in 2013

00:02:58.028 --> 00:03:00.104
but the prices have
gone down substantially

00:03:00.104 --> 00:03:04.264
in the past few years and
by 2023 Dr. Mark Post hopes

00:03:04.264 --> 00:03:07.712
that you'll be buying lab grown
meat at supermarket prices.

00:03:07.712 --> 00:03:10.257
- If it tastes good and it looks like

00:03:10.257 --> 00:03:13.043
they're doing it responsibly,

00:03:13.043 --> 00:03:14.374
I have no problems with it.

00:03:14.374 --> 00:03:16.417
- Hell yeah I'd eat lab grown meat.

00:03:16.417 --> 00:03:17.730
That sounds dope.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:19.770
Meat's delicious, everyone knows that

00:03:19.770 --> 00:03:21.494
unless you're not into meat.

00:03:21.494 --> 00:03:24.878
- There is quite some
flavor with the browning

00:03:24.878 --> 00:03:27.214
and I know there is no fat in it,

00:03:27.214 --> 00:03:31.509
so I didn't really know how
it's, how juicy it will be.

00:03:31.509 --> 00:03:34.755
- Lab grown meat lacks the fat
from traditional livestock,

00:03:34.755 --> 00:03:37.763
so unless you're super into lean meat,

00:03:37.763 --> 00:03:39.951
the taste might not be your thing.

00:03:39.951 --> 00:03:41.875
- But there is quite some intense taste.

00:03:41.875 --> 00:03:45.911
It's close to meat, it's not that juicy.

00:03:45.911 --> 00:03:48.255
- The good news is that
scientists are experimenting

00:03:48.255 --> 00:03:51.155
on ways to add healthy
fats into lab grown meat

00:03:51.155 --> 00:03:54.021
so you can get that
juicy taste you desire.

00:03:54.021 --> 00:03:56.646
♫ Mm juicy taste

00:03:56.646 --> 00:03:59.348
But the bottom line is
if I walked up to you

00:03:59.348 --> 00:04:02.858
with a hamburger, that was
made out of lab grown meat,

00:04:02.858 --> 00:04:04.823
would you try it?

00:04:04.823 --> 00:04:06.656
- Man if this lab grown
meat thing works out,

00:04:06.656 --> 00:04:08.196
it would be very exciting.

00:04:08.196 --> 00:04:09.537
I mean I love--

00:04:09.537 --> 00:04:12.370
- One Earth, one people, so people

00:04:13.306 --> 00:04:15.231
make it in a lab.

00:04:15.231 --> 00:04:16.398
- That's true.

